{# The layout of the pages of the bundle, overridden by the application to give them their look
   (architecture §5.2, §6): the same document and the same blocks as the layout of the bundle, one
   stylesheet built from assets/styles/app.css (Tailwind and DaisyUI), no script. The pages of the
   bundle come with it untouched: what they render is styled by its structure and its data-* codes.

   Two shapes, because the pages are of two kinds. A page of an interaction asks one thing of whoever is
   in front of it, a login, a consent, a code typed from an appliance, and nothing else is on it: a box in
   the middle of the screen is what that is. A page of the account is a page someone reads and comes back
   to, holding a list, a table, a heading and the way back: it takes the width of a column of text, at the
   top of the screen, and carries "account" on its main so the stylesheet can say what a panel looks like
   there. Which one a request is, is its route (architecture §5.4).

   The theme is on the document and not in a script (issue #447): light and dark are what the stylesheet
   declares, and a document that names neither leaves the answer to the browser. #}
{% set account = (app.request.attributes.get('_route') ?? '') starts with 'beffroi_interaction_account' %}
{% set chosen_theme = theme() %}
{# The colours the tenant declared (issue beffroi-php/beffroi#449), written on the document as the two
   custom properties DaisyUI draws a primary surface from: the accent of the buttons and the links, and
   the colour of what is written on them. They are on the document and not in the stylesheet because the
   stylesheet is built once for the deployment and these come from a row. The value is three or six
   hexadecimal digits, which is all the model lets a tenant say, so there is nothing else it could put in
   this attribute; a tenant that declared no colour leaves the attribute off and the themes answer. #}
{% set tenant = beffroi_tenant() %}
{% set colored = tenant is not null and tenant.primaryColor is not null %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html
    lang="{{ app.request.locale|replace({'_': '-'}) }}"
    {%- if chosen_theme.attribute() is not null %} data-theme="{{ chosen_theme.attribute() }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if colored %} style="--color-primary: {{ tenant.primaryColor }}; --color-primary-content: {{ tenant.primaryContentColor }}"{% endif %}
>
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{% block title %}{% endblock %}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/app.css') }}">
    {% block head %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body class="{{ account ? 'min-h-dvh bg-base-200' : 'min-h-dvh bg-base-200 grid place-items-center p-4' }}">
    {# The two controls of a page: the language, which the bundle ships as structure and words and this
       stylesheet dresses, and the theme, which is this application's alone (issues #448 and #447). Where
       they sit follows the shape of the page, which is why they are rendered once and placed twice. #}
    {% set controls %}
        {% include '@Beffroi/_locale_switcher.html.twig' %}
        {% include '_theme_switcher.html.twig' %}
    {% endset %}
    {# The logo of the tenant, which the bundle ships as a header with its name as alternative text (issue
       beffroi-php/beffroi#449): it heads the column of a page of the account, beside the controls, and
       sits above the box of a page of an interaction, where whoever is in front of the screen reads who
       they came for before reading the question. A tenant that declared no logo renders nothing, and the
       page is the one it was. Rendered once and placed twice, as the controls are. #}
    {% set brand %}{% include '@Beffroi/_brand.html.twig' %}{% endset %}
    {% if account %}
        {# A page of the account is a column someone reads: the controls head that column, aligned with it
           and scrolling with it, rather than floating over its heading. #}
        <div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl items-center justify-between gap-2 px-4 pt-6 sm:px-6">
            {{ brand }}
            <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-2">{{ controls }}</div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% block body %}
        {% if not account %}{{ brand }}{% endif %}
        <main
            {% if account %}data-page="account"{% endif %}
            class="{{ account ? 'mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl flex-col gap-5 px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14' : 'card card-body w-full max-w-md bg-base-100 shadow-xl' }}"
        >
            <h1 class="{{ account ? 'text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl' : 'card-title text-2xl' }}">{% block heading %}{{ block('title') }}{% endblock %}</h1>
            {% block content %}{% endblock %}
        </main>
    {% endblock %}
    {% if not account %}
        {# A page of an interaction is one box in the middle of an empty screen, so the two controls take a
           corner of it: the top one, the bottom of the screen being the web debug toolbar in development. #}
        <div class="fixed top-4 right-4 z-10 flex items-center gap-2">{{ controls }}</div>
    {% endif %}
</body>
</html>
